  "seven_q": {
    "Q0_posture": "Analytical and exploratory: the document examines a proposed isomorphism between quantum superposition/collapse and theological mystery/revelation, with rigorous testing and honest acknowledgment of strains.",
    "Q1_identity": "An isomorphism record (ISO-011) that maps quantum superposition and wavefunction collapse to theological mystery and revelation, including mathematical formulations, test protocols, and strain analysis.",
    "Q2_domain": "Intersection of quantum physics, Christian theology, information theory, and philosophy of science.",
    "Q3_claim": "There is a structural isomorphism between quantum superposition/collapse and theological mystery/revelation, characterized by a shared process topology of indefinite\u2192definite\u2192irreversible, with a testable prediction (E6.2) that collapse rate depends on observer coherence.",
    "Q4_support": "Mathematical formulations of superposition and collapse, Landauer bound, modified Schr\u00f6dinger equation (E6.2), scriptural evidence (Colossians 1:26-27, Hebrews 7:27, etc.), and connections to 7 other ISOs.",
    "Q5_dependencies": "Copenhagen interpretation of quantum mechanics, Landauer's principle, modified Schr\u00f6dinger equation (E6.2), Christian doctrine of revelation and ephapax, and the broader isomorphism framework.",
    "Q6_consequences": "If confirmed, it would establish a genuine cross-domain structural parallel with predictive power; if falsified, it retreats to analogy. It also implies that revelation has a thermodynamic-like cost and that observer coherence affects collapse rates.",
    "Q7_kill": "Experimental falsification of E6.2 (\u03a6-independent collapse rate), proof that collapse is reversible, demonstration that OT prophecy was always univocal, or confirmation of many-worlds interpretation (no collapse)."
  },
